# KibbiSave brand color & glass

Before writing or changing any UI (HTML/CSS/JS), follow these tokens from `css/kibbisave-site.css` (mirror under `public/css/`). Do not invent new blues or flat primary fills.

## Core tokens (light)

| Token | Value / role |
|-------|----------------|
| `--kb-primary` | `#00008b` — brand navy for words, numbers, links, icons |
| `--kb-primary-mid` / `--kb-msg-to` | `#0a0aff` — slightly lighter navy |
| `--kb-msg-from` | `#00008b` |
| `--kb-msg-gradient` | dark navy → slightly lighter navy (148deg) |
| `--kb-msg-shadow` | soft navy action shadow |
| `--kb-navy` | `#00008b` — solid chrome (bottom nav, heroes); **never** remaps to cream |
| `--kb-heading` | same family as `--kb-primary` |
| `--kb-glass-bg` | translucent frosted surface |
| `--kb-glass-border` | `rgba(0, 0, 139, 0.1)` |
| `--kb-glass-blur` | `blur(14px)` |

Dark mode remaps primary/msg tokens to cream — keep using variables; do not hardcode cream hex in feature CSS unless matching existing dark patterns.

## Message & action buttons

- Prefer class `kb-msg-btn` (also `.mp-action--msg`, `.msg-send`, `.cd-dm-send`, Join/Deposit/Create CTAs).
- Fill = `var(--kb-msg-gradient)` — **#00008b → #0a0aff**, not flat `#00008b` alone, not purple/indigo kits.
- Text on light: white. Dark: `--kb-cta-ink` via shared site CSS.
- Shadow: `var(--kb-msg-shadow)`.

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.btn { background: #3b82f6; }
.btn { background: #00008b; }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.btn {
  background: var(--kb-msg-gradient);
  color: #fff;
  box-shadow: var(--kb-msg-shadow);
}
```

## Words & numbers in blue

Amounts, ranks, message authors, active tab labels, race cues, profile totals → `color: var(--kb-primary)`.

## Glass surfaces

Cards, message panels, sheets, member-profile sections:

- `background: var(--kb-glass-bg)`
- `border: 1px solid var(--kb-glass-border)`
- `backdrop-filter: var(--kb-glass-blur)` (+ `-webkit-backdrop-filter`)
- Or classes `kb-glass` / `kb-glass-soft`

Solid navy heroes/nav chrome use `--kb-navy`, not glass and not msg-gradient.

## Community / group parity

- Both use **Member standings** + **Messages** tabs.
- Member charts and channel messages are **members-only**; guests get login/join gates.
- Sync root and `public/` copies of HTML/CSS/JS when they diverge.

## File touchpoints

- Tokens: `css/kibbisave-site.css` (+ `public/css/…`)
- Community: `kibbisave_cause_detail.html`
